                <pb facs="0340" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.113/109a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France (Edge)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-17T14:00:00-04:00">September 17, 1932—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. The copper interests are anxious to obtain relief from the discrimination in
                    favor of Belgium. Has there been any recent progress in this matter?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
